{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781016759,"nonce":"S0aflvIodYdLev9jT3vH0M+QB7M=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABE45B3A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/243","origin":"github"},"title":"izzyboat.rviz subscribes to /izzy/hover_visualization as Marker, not MarkerArray — breaks rosbag2 recording","message":"## Problem\n\nSame class of bug as ben_project11#26 (and its fix PR rolker/ben_project11#27), on the Izzy config: `ros2 bag record` will reject `/izzy/hover_visualization` with\n\n```\n[ROSBAG2_TRANSPORT]: Topic '/izzy/hover_visualization' has more than one type associated. Only topics with one type are supported\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe hover behavior publisher (`behavior_server`, from `unh_marine_navigation`) emits `visualization_msgs/msg/MarkerArray`. But the **\"Hover Marker\"** display in `izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.rviz` (line 381) is class `rviz_default_plugins/Marker` — it subscribes as `Marker`. That second type announcement on the topic name makes rosbag2 (which enforces type-uniqueness across **all** endpoints, publishers and subscribers) reject the topic.\n\nCAMP is not at fault — its marker subscription is type-adaptive and mirrors whatever type is on the graph; correcting rviz leaves `MarkerArray` as the only type and CAMP adapts automatically.\n\nbizzy is unaffected: there is no `bizzyboat.rviz` (bizzy is CAMP-driven), so only `izzyboat.rviz` carries the display.\n\n## Fix\n\n`izzyboat_project11/config/izzyboat.rviz`: change the \"Hover Marker\" display from `rviz_default_plugins/Marker` to `rviz_default_plugins/MarkerArray`.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}